/* Long, child-friendly stories for the Places tab ("Read the story").
   Keys match the place names in SEERAH (index.html). Each story:
     img:  photo ids in img/ (first = top photo, second = halfway down)
     en/ms: cap  = one caption per photo
            p    = paragraphs, short sentences for a young reader
            look = things to spot when you are there
            think = one question to talk about together
   Sources: the Quran, Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim where a hadith is quoted;
   a few well-known seerah details (Ibn Ishaq) are marked "The seerah books tell". */
