const STORIES={
"Masjid Al-Haram":{img:["kaaba-wide","haram-1886"],
 en:{cap:["Masjid Al-Haram today. The Kaaba is the small black cube in the middle.","A drawing of Masjid Al-Haram in 1886. See the old arches behind the Kaaba? Look how different it was!"],
 p:["Masjid Al-Haram is the big masjid all around the Kaaba. The Kaaba is the house in the middle. The masjid is everything around it: the open floor where people do tawaf, the halls, the floors above, and the courtyards.",
 "It is the oldest masjid on earth. Abu Dharr asked the Prophet ﷺ which masjid was built first. He said: “Al-Masjid Al-Haram.” Then which? “Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa.” And how long between them? “40 years.” (Bukhari)",
 "“Haram” here means sacred and protected. Allah made Makkah a safe place from the day He created the heavens and the earth. Inside its borders, nobody may hunt, cut down its trees, or even chase a bird out of the shade so they can sit there. (Bukhari) That is why the pigeons here are so tame!",
 "Praying here is extra special. The Prophet ﷺ said that one prayer in Masjid Al-Haram is better than 100,000 prayers anywhere else. (Ahmad, Ibn Majah) So every prayer you pray here counts for a lot.",
 "The Night Journey started here. One night, Allah took the Prophet ﷺ from Masjid Al-Haram to Masjid Al-Aqsa in Jerusalem, and then up through the heavens. (Al-Isra' 17:1)",
 "In the Prophet's ﷺ time there were no walls at all. The houses of Makkah came right up to the open space around the Kaaba. When Makkah grew busy, Umar, the second khalifah, bought some of the houses and built a low wall around the space. Then Uthman made it bigger. That was the start of the masjid as a building.",
 "Over hundreds of years, different rulers made it bigger and bigger. The Ottoman Turks built rows of small domes and arches around the courtyard. You can see them in the old picture, and some of them are still standing today.",
 "Today it is the biggest masjid in the world. Millions of people can pray here at once, on many floors and in huge new halls. The white marble on the floor is a special kind that stays cool, even in the hot sun, so you can walk on it barefoot.",
 "Every hour of every day, day and night, someone is doing tawaf around the Kaaba. It almost never stops."],
 look:["The old Ottoman arches and small domes, next to the newer white halls.","The pigeons. They are protected here, so never chase them.","The gate numbers. Remember the number of the gate you came in by, so you can find your family.","The cool white marble floor around the Kaaba."],
 think:"Every prayer here counts like 100,000. Which prayer will you try hardest to pray in Masjid Al-Haram?"},
 ms:{cap:["Masjidil Haram hari ini. Kaabah ialah kiub hitam kecil di tengah-tengah.","Lukisan Masjidil Haram pada tahun 1886. Nampak gerbang lama di belakang Kaabah? Lihat betapa berbezanya dahulu!"],
 p:["Masjidil Haram ialah masjid besar yang mengelilingi Kaabah. Kaabah ialah rumah di tengah-tengahnya. Masjid pula ialah segala yang ada di sekelilingnya: lantai terbuka tempat orang bertawaf, dewan-dewan, tingkat-tingkat di atas, dan halamannya.",
 "Inilah masjid tertua di muka bumi. Abu Dzar bertanya kepada Nabi ﷺ, masjid manakah yang mula-mula dibina. Baginda menjawab: “Al-Masjid Al-Haram.” Kemudian yang mana? “Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa.” Berapa lama jarak antara keduanya? “40 tahun.” (Bukhari)",
 "“Haram” di sini bermaksud suci dan dilindungi. Allah menjadikan Makkah tempat yang aman sejak hari Dia mencipta langit dan bumi. Di dalam sempadannya, tiada siapa boleh memburu, menebang pokoknya, malah menghalau burung dari tempat teduh supaya dia boleh duduk di situ pun tidak boleh. (Bukhari) Sebab itulah burung merpati di sini sangat jinak!",
 "Solat di sini sangat istimewa. Nabi ﷺ bersabda bahawa satu solat di Masjidil Haram lebih baik daripada 100,000 solat di tempat lain. (Ahmad, Ibn Majah) Jadi setiap solat yang anda dirikan di sini bernilai sangat besar.",
 "Perjalanan Isra' bermula di sini. Pada suatu malam, Allah membawa Nabi ﷺ dari Masjidil Haram ke Masjidil Aqsa di Baitulmaqdis, kemudian naik ke langit. (Al-Isra' 17:1)",
 "Pada zaman Nabi ﷺ, tiada dinding langsung. Rumah-rumah di Makkah terletak betul-betul di tepi kawasan lapang di sekeliling Kaabah. Apabila Makkah semakin sesak, Saidina Umar, khalifah kedua, membeli sebahagian rumah itu dan membina tembok rendah di sekeliling kawasan itu. Kemudian Saidina Uthman membesarkannya. Itulah permulaan masjid sebagai sebuah bangunan.",
 "Selama ratusan tahun, pemerintah demi pemerintah membesarkannya lagi dan lagi. Orang Turki Uthmaniyah membina deretan kubah kecil dan gerbang di sekeliling halaman. Anda boleh melihatnya dalam gambar lama itu, dan sebahagiannya masih berdiri hingga hari ini.",
 "Hari ini, inilah masjid terbesar di dunia. Berjuta-juta orang boleh bersolat di sini serentak, di banyak tingkat dan di dewan-dewan baharu yang sangat besar. Marmar putih di lantainya jenis istimewa yang kekal sejuk walaupun di bawah matahari panas, jadi anda boleh berjalan di atasnya tanpa kasut.",
 "Setiap jam, siang dan malam, ada orang yang sedang bertawaf mengelilingi Kaabah. Tawaf hampir tidak pernah berhenti."],
 look:["Gerbang dan kubah kecil Uthmaniyah yang lama, di sebelah dewan putih yang lebih baharu.","Burung merpati. Mereka dilindungi di sini, jadi jangan sekali-kali mengejarnya.","Nombor pintu. Ingat nombor pintu yang anda masuk, supaya mudah mencari keluarga.","Lantai marmar putih yang sejuk di sekeliling Kaabah."],
 think:"Setiap solat di sini bernilai seperti 100,000 solat. Solat yang mana akan anda cuba bersungguh-sungguh dirikan di Masjidil Haram?"}},

"The Kaaba":{img:["kaaba"],
 en:{cap:["The Kaaba, with pilgrims walking around it in tawaf."],
 p:["A long, long time ago, Allah told Prophet Ibrahim to build a house where people could worship Him alone. Ibrahim and his son Ismail built it together, right here in Makkah.",
 "Ismail carried the stones and Ibrahim placed them, one by one. When the walls grew too high to reach, Ibrahim stood on a big stone to keep building. That stone is still here today. It is called Maqam Ibrahim.",
 "While they worked, they made a dua: “Our Lord, accept this from us. You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.” (Al-Baqarah 2:127)",
 "The Kaaba is shaped like a cube. In fact, “Kaaba” comes from the Arabic word for cube. It wears a black cloth called the kiswah, with verses of the Quran sewn on in gold-coloured thread. It gets a brand-new kiswah every year.",
 "Many years later, a flood damaged the Kaaba and the people of Makkah, the Quraysh, rebuilt it. When it was time to put the Black Stone back in its corner, the tribes began to argue. Every tribe wanted the honour! They nearly started a fight.",
 "They agreed to let the next man who walked in decide. It was Muhammad ﷺ, who was 35 and not yet a prophet. Everyone was happy, because they called him Al-Amin: the one you can trust.",
 "He spread out a cloth and put the Black Stone in the middle. Then he asked a leader from every tribe to hold one edge. Together they lifted it up, and he set it in the wall with his own hands. Everyone helped, and nobody fought.",
 "When the Prophet ﷺ came back to Makkah in the year 8 AH, there were 360 idols around the Kaaba. He knocked them down with a stick, reciting: “The truth has come and falsehood has gone.” (Al-Isra' 17:81) Since that day, the Kaaba has been for Allah alone.",
 "Today, wherever Muslims are in the world, they face the Kaaba when they pray. When you pray at home, you are facing this very building!"],
 look:["The Black Stone, in a silver frame on one corner. Tawaf starts there.","Maqam Ibrahim, inside a gold and glass case near the Kaaba.","The Kaaba door, made of gold, high above the ground.","Hijr Ismail, the low curved wall. It is part of the Kaaba, so tawaf goes around it, never through it.","The golden rain spout on the roof, called the Mizab."],
 think:"The Prophet ﷺ stopped a fight by finding a way for everyone to help. Next time your friends argue, how could you include everyone?"},
 ms:{cap:["Kaabah, dengan jemaah yang berjalan mengelilinginya ketika tawaf."],
 p:["Dahulu kala, Allah menyuruh Nabi Ibrahim membina sebuah rumah supaya manusia boleh menyembah-Nya sahaja. Nabi Ibrahim dan anaknya, Nabi Ismail, membinanya bersama-sama, di sini di Makkah.",
 "Nabi Ismail mengangkat batu dan Nabi Ibrahim menyusunnya, satu demi satu. Apabila dinding sudah terlalu tinggi untuk dicapai, Nabi Ibrahim berdiri di atas sebuah batu besar untuk terus membina. Batu itu masih ada di sini hingga hari ini. Namanya Makam Ibrahim.",
 "Sambil bekerja, mereka berdoa: “Wahai Tuhan kami, terimalah daripada kami. Sesungguhnya Engkaulah Yang Maha Mendengar, lagi Maha Mengetahui.” (Al-Baqarah 2:127)",
 "Kaabah berbentuk kiub. Malah, perkataan “Kaabah” datang daripada perkataan Arab yang bermaksud kiub. Kaabah memakai kain hitam yang dipanggil kiswah, dengan ayat-ayat al-Quran dijahit dengan benang berwarna emas. Kaabah mendapat kiswah baharu setiap tahun.",
 "Bertahun-tahun kemudian, banjir merosakkan Kaabah, lalu penduduk Makkah, iaitu kaum Quraisy, membinanya semula. Apabila tiba masa untuk meletakkan semula Hajarul Aswad di penjurunya, kabilah-kabilah mula bertengkar. Setiap kabilah mahukan penghormatan itu! Mereka hampir bergaduh.",
 "Mereka bersetuju untuk membiarkan lelaki pertama yang masuk selepas itu membuat keputusan. Orang itu ialah Muhammad ﷺ, yang berumur 35 tahun dan belum lagi menjadi nabi. Semua orang gembira, kerana mereka menggelarnya Al-Amin: orang yang boleh dipercayai.",
 "Baginda membentangkan sehelai kain dan meletakkan Hajarul Aswad di tengah-tengahnya. Kemudian baginda meminta seorang ketua daripada setiap kabilah memegang satu tepi kain itu. Bersama-sama mereka mengangkatnya, dan baginda meletakkannya di dinding dengan tangan baginda sendiri. Semua orang membantu, dan tiada siapa yang bergaduh.",
 "Apabila Nabi ﷺ kembali ke Makkah pada tahun 8 H, terdapat 360 berhala di sekeliling Kaabah. Baginda menjatuhkannya dengan sebatang tongkat sambil membaca: “Kebenaran telah datang dan kebatilan telah lenyap.” (Al-Isra' 17:81) Sejak hari itu, Kaabah hanya untuk Allah.",
 "Hari ini, di mana-mana sahaja umat Islam berada di dunia, mereka menghadap Kaabah ketika solat. Apabila kamu solat di rumah, kamu sedang menghadap bangunan inilah!"],
 look:["Hajarul Aswad, dalam bingkai perak di salah satu penjuru. Tawaf bermula di situ.","Makam Ibrahim, di dalam bekas emas dan kaca berhampiran Kaabah.","Pintu Kaabah, diperbuat daripada emas, tinggi dari tanah.","Hijir Ismail, dinding rendah yang melengkung. Ia sebahagian daripada Kaabah, jadi tawaf mengelilinginya, bukan melaluinya.","Saluran air hujan berwarna emas di atas bumbung, dipanggil Mizab (Pancur Emas)."],
 think:"Nabi ﷺ menghentikan pergaduhan dengan mencari cara supaya semua orang dapat membantu. Lain kali kawan-kawan kamu bertengkar, bagaimana kamu boleh libatkan semua orang?"}},

"Safa, Marwah and Zamzam":{img:["sai","masa"],
 en:{cap:["Pilgrims doing sa'i between Safa and Marwah.","The long hall of sa'i. Long ago this was an empty, rocky valley."],
 p:["Prophet Ibrahim brought his wife Hajar and their baby Ismail to this valley. Back then there were no buildings, no trees, no water and no people. Only rocks and hot sun.",
 "Ibrahim left them a bag of dates and some water, and began to walk away. Hajar ran after him. “Are you leaving us here, where there is nobody and nothing?” He did not answer. So she asked: “Did Allah tell you to do this?” He said yes. Then Hajar said: “Then Allah will not let us be lost.” What strong trust she had!",
 "When he was out of sight, Ibrahim raised his hands and prayed: “Our Lord, I have settled some of my family in a valley with no crops, near Your Sacred House... so make people's hearts love them, and give them fruits.” (Ibrahim 14:37)",
 "Soon the water ran out. Baby Ismail cried and cried with thirst. Hajar could not bear to watch. She climbed the nearest hill, Safa, and looked all around for water or for people. Nothing.",
 "She hurried down into the valley and up the other hill, Marwah, and looked again. Nothing. Back and forth she went, 7 times.",
 "On Marwah, she heard a sound. It was the angel Jibril! He struck the ground, and water burst out. Hajar quickly built a little wall of sand around it to keep it in, and filled her water skin. That water is Zamzam, and it has never stopped flowing, for thousands of years.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ later said: “May Allah have mercy on the mother of Ismail! If she had left Zamzam alone, it would have become a flowing stream.” (Bukhari)",
 "Birds started to circle over the water. A tribe passing by, called Jurhum, saw the birds and knew there must be water. They asked Hajar if they could live there, and that is how Makkah began to grow into a town. (Bukhari)",
 "Allah made Hajar's running part of worship forever (Al-Baqarah 2:158). Every Umrah ends with sa'i: walking 7 times between Safa and Marwah, just like her. Between the green lights, men jog a little, where Hajar hurried across the low valley."],
 look:["The real rock of Safa, under the small dome at the start of sa'i.","The green lights on the ceiling. Men jog between them.","Zamzam taps and coolers all around the masjid. Say Bismillah, drink, and make a dua."],
 think:"Hajar kept trying, even when she found nothing 6 times. Allah's help came while she was still trying. What is something you should keep trying at?"},
 ms:{cap:["Jemaah melakukan saie antara Safa dan Marwah.","Dewan saie yang panjang. Dahulu, tempat ini ialah lembah kosong yang berbatu."],
 p:["Nabi Ibrahim membawa isterinya Siti Hajar dan bayi mereka, Nabi Ismail, ke lembah ini. Pada masa itu tiada bangunan, tiada pokok, tiada air dan tiada manusia. Hanya batu dan matahari yang panas.",
 "Nabi Ibrahim meninggalkan untuk mereka seuncang kurma dan sedikit air, lalu mula berjalan pergi. Siti Hajar berlari mengejarnya. “Adakah kamu meninggalkan kami di sini, tempat yang tiada sesiapa dan tiada apa-apa?” Baginda tidak menjawab. Jadi Siti Hajar bertanya: “Adakah Allah yang menyuruh kamu berbuat begini?” Baginda menjawab ya. Lalu Siti Hajar berkata: “Kalau begitu, Allah tidak akan mensia-siakan kami.” Kuatnya kepercayaannya kepada Allah!",
 "Apabila sudah tidak kelihatan, Nabi Ibrahim mengangkat tangan dan berdoa: “Wahai Tuhan kami, aku telah menempatkan sebahagian keluargaku di sebuah lembah yang tiada tanaman, dekat Rumah-Mu yang suci... maka jadikanlah hati manusia cinta kepada mereka, dan kurniakanlah mereka buah-buahan.” (Ibrahim 14:37)",
 "Tidak lama kemudian, air pun habis. Bayi Ismail menangis dan terus menangis kerana dahaga. Siti Hajar tidak sanggup melihatnya. Dia mendaki bukit yang paling dekat, Safa, dan melihat ke sekeliling mencari air atau manusia. Tiada apa-apa.",
 "Dia bergegas turun ke lembah dan naik ke bukit yang satu lagi, Marwah, lalu melihat lagi. Tiada apa-apa. Dia berulang-alik sebanyak 7 kali.",
 "Di Marwah, dia terdengar satu bunyi. Itulah malaikat Jibril! Jibril memukul tanah, lalu air memancut keluar. Siti Hajar cepat-cepat membina dinding pasir kecil di sekelilingnya supaya air itu tidak mengalir pergi, dan mengisi bekas airnya. Air itulah Zamzam, dan ia tidak pernah berhenti mengalir, selama beribu-ribu tahun.",
 "Rasulullah ﷺ kemudian bersabda: “Semoga Allah merahmati ibu Ismail! Kalaulah dia membiarkan Zamzam itu, tentu ia menjadi sungai yang mengalir.” (Bukhari)",
 "Burung-burung mula terbang berpusing di atas air itu. Satu kabilah yang lalu di situ, bernama Jurhum, ternampak burung-burung itu dan tahu mesti ada air. Mereka bertanya kepada Siti Hajar jika mereka boleh tinggal di situ, dan begitulah Makkah mula membesar menjadi sebuah bandar. (Bukhari)",
 "Allah menjadikan larian Siti Hajar sebahagian daripada ibadah untuk selama-lamanya (Al-Baqarah 2:158). Setiap umrah berakhir dengan saie: berjalan 7 kali antara Safa dan Marwah, sama seperti dia. Di antara lampu hijau, lelaki berlari-lari anak sedikit, di tempat Siti Hajar bergegas melintasi lembah yang rendah."],
 look:["Batu sebenar bukit Safa, di bawah kubah kecil di permulaan saie.","Lampu hijau di siling. Lelaki berlari-lari anak di antaranya.","Paip dan bekas air Zamzam di sekeliling masjid. Baca Bismillah, minum, dan berdoa."],
 think:"Siti Hajar terus mencuba, walaupun 6 kali dia tidak menjumpai apa-apa. Pertolongan Allah datang ketika dia masih berusaha. Apakah sesuatu yang kamu patut terus cuba?"}},

"Jabal Nour · Cave Hira":{img:["hira","hira-cave"],
 en:{cap:["Jabal Nour, the Mountain of Light. The cave is near the top.","The small opening of Cave Hira."],
 p:["Jabal Nour means “the Mountain of Light”. Near its top is a tiny cave called Hira. It is so small that only a few people can fit inside.",
 "Before he became a prophet, Muhammad ﷺ was sad about the wrong things people in Makkah did, like praying to idols and being unkind to the poor. So he would climb up here and stay for many days, thinking and worshipping Allah. His wife Khadijah packed him food, and he came home to get more.",
 "One night in Ramadan, when he was 40 years old, the angel Jibril came into the cave and said: “Iqra'!” It means “Read!”",
 "He answered: “I cannot read.” Jibril held him tight, let go, and said again: “Read!” This happened 3 times. Then Jibril recited the very first words of the Quran: “Read in the name of your Lord who created. He created man from a clinging clot. Read! Your Lord is the Most Generous, who taught by the pen.” (Al-'Alaq 96:1–5)",
 "These were the first verses of the Quran ever revealed. Over the next 23 years, the rest of the Quran came down, a little at a time.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ hurried home, trembling, and said: “Cover me! Cover me!” Khadijah wrapped him in a blanket until he felt calm. Then she said kind, brave words: “Allah will never let you down. You are good to your family, you help the weak, you welcome guests, and you help people in trouble.” (Bukhari)",
 "She took him to her cousin Waraqah, a wise old man who knew the earlier holy books. Waraqah said it was the same angel who had come to Prophet Musa.",
 "Climbing the mountain is not part of Umrah. The path has hundreds of steps and takes about an hour. If you climb it, bring water, go when it is cool, and stay close to your family."],
 look:["The mountain's pointed top, like a hump, from the road.","From up high, the towers of Makkah and the clock tower.","Cave Hira itself, a gap between big rocks."],
 think:"The very first word of the Quran was “Read!” That is why learning is so important in Islam. What would you love to learn more about?"},
 ms:{cap:["Jabal Nur, Bukit Cahaya. Gua itu berada berhampiran puncaknya.","Pintu masuk Gua Hira yang kecil."],
 p:["Jabal Nur bermaksud “Bukit Cahaya”. Berhampiran puncaknya ada sebuah gua yang sangat kecil bernama Hira. Gua itu begitu kecil sehingga hanya beberapa orang sahaja boleh muat di dalamnya.",
 "Sebelum menjadi nabi, Muhammad ﷺ berasa sedih dengan perbuatan salah penduduk Makkah, seperti menyembah berhala dan tidak berbuat baik kepada orang miskin. Jadi baginda selalu mendaki ke sini dan tinggal selama beberapa hari, berfikir dan beribadah kepada Allah. Isteri baginda, Khadijah, menyediakan bekalan makanan, dan baginda pulang ke rumah untuk mengambil bekalan lagi.",
 "Pada suatu malam di bulan Ramadan, ketika baginda berumur 40 tahun, malaikat Jibril datang ke dalam gua dan berkata: “Iqra'!” Maksudnya “Bacalah!”",
 "Baginda menjawab: “Aku tidak tahu membaca.” Jibril memeluk baginda dengan erat, melepaskannya, dan berkata lagi: “Bacalah!” Perkara ini berlaku 3 kali. Kemudian Jibril membacakan kata-kata pertama al-Quran: “Bacalah dengan nama Tuhanmu yang menciptakan. Dia menciptakan manusia daripada segumpal darah. Bacalah! Dan Tuhanmu Yang Maha Pemurah, yang mengajar dengan pena.” (Al-'Alaq 96:1–5)",
 "Inilah ayat-ayat al-Quran yang pertama sekali diturunkan. Dalam 23 tahun selepas itu, ayat-ayat yang lain pula turun, sedikit demi sedikit.",
 "Nabi ﷺ bergegas pulang dalam keadaan menggigil, dan berkata: “Selimutkan aku! Selimutkan aku!” Khadijah menyelimutkan baginda sehingga baginda berasa tenang. Kemudian Khadijah mengucapkan kata-kata yang baik dan berani: “Allah tidak akan sekali-kali mengecewakan kamu. Kamu berbuat baik kepada keluarga, kamu membantu orang yang lemah, kamu memuliakan tetamu, dan kamu menolong orang yang dalam kesusahan.” (Bukhari)",
 "Khadijah membawa baginda berjumpa sepupunya, Waraqah, seorang lelaki tua yang bijak dan mengetahui kitab-kitab suci yang terdahulu. Waraqah berkata itulah malaikat yang sama yang pernah datang kepada Nabi Musa.",
 "Mendaki bukit ini bukan sebahagian daripada umrah. Laluannya ada beratus-ratus anak tangga dan mengambil masa kira-kira sejam. Jika kamu mendakinya, bawa air, pergi ketika cuaca sejuk, dan sentiasa dekat dengan keluarga kamu."],
 look:["Puncak bukit yang tajam, seperti bonggol, dilihat dari jalan raya.","Dari atas, menara-menara di Makkah dan menara jam.","Gua Hira sendiri, satu celah di antara batu-batu besar."],
 think:"Perkataan pertama al-Quran ialah “Bacalah!” Sebab itulah belajar sangat penting dalam Islam. Apakah yang kamu sangat ingin pelajari dengan lebih lanjut?"}},

"Jabal Thur":{img:["thur"],
 en:{cap:["Jabal Thur, seen from the road. The cave is near the top."],
 p:["When the people of Makkah kept hurting the Muslims, Allah allowed them to move to the city of Madinah. This journey is called the Hijrah. The Islamic calendar starts from the year it happened!",
 "The leaders of Makkah made an evil plan to attack the Prophet ﷺ at night. Allah told him about it. The seerah books tell that Ali slept in his bed that night, while the Prophet ﷺ slipped away safely.",
 "He and his best friend Abu Bakr did not go north towards Madinah. They went south, the opposite way, to this mountain, Thur. They hid in a small cave near the top. Clever, right?",
 "The Quraysh were furious. They promised 100 camels to anyone who caught them. Searchers climbed all the way up, right to the mouth of the cave! Abu Bakr could see their feet. He whispered: “If one of them looks down at his feet, he will see us!”",
 "The Prophet ﷺ answered calmly: “What do you think of two, when Allah is the third with them?” (Bukhari, Muslim) Allah tells this story in the Quran: “Do not be sad. Allah is with us.” (At-Tawbah 9:40) The searchers turned around and left.",
 "You may have heard that a spider spun a web across the mouth of the cave, so the searchers thought no one could have gone in. This is in Musnad Ahmad. Some scholars, like Ibn Kathir and Ibn Hajar, said it is fair, and others said its chain is weak. Stories of two doves nesting at the entrance are weaker still.",
 "Another story many people tell: Abu Bakr went in first and blocked the holes in the cave with pieces of his cloth. The Prophet ﷺ fell asleep with his head on Abu Bakr's lap. A snake bit Abu Bakr's foot from the last hole, but he did not move, so he would not wake his friend. His tears fell on the Prophet's ﷺ face. The Prophet ﷺ woke, put a little of his saliva on the bite, and the pain went away. Scholars say this story's chain is weak, so we tell it as a story, not as something certain. What we know for sure, from the Quran and Bukhari, is that Allah kept them safe.",
 "They stayed in the cave for 3 nights. Each evening, Abu Bakr's son Abdullah crept up to tell them the news from Makkah. A shepherd, Amir ibn Fuhayrah, brought his sheep past the cave so they could drink fresh milk, and the sheep's hooves covered up the footprints! (Bukhari)",
 "Abu Bakr's daughter Asma' brought them food for the journey. She had nothing to tie the bag with, so she tore her waist belt in two and used one half. After that she was called “the one with two belts”. (Bukhari)",
 "After 3 days, when the searching died down, a guide brought camels, and they set off for Madinah by a secret road along the coast.",
 "The mountain is very high and the climb is hard, so most people see it from below."],
 look:["The tall, rocky peak. Try to imagine climbing it at night, with no path.","How far Thur is from the Kaaba. They went the opposite way from Madinah!"],
 think:"Abu Bakr was scared, but the Prophet ﷺ reminded him that Allah was with them. When you feel scared, what could you say to yourself?"},
 ms:{cap:["Jabal Thur, dilihat dari jalan raya. Gua itu berada berhampiran puncaknya."],
 p:["Apabila penduduk Makkah terus menyakiti orang Islam, Allah membenarkan mereka berpindah ke bandar Madinah. Perjalanan ini dipanggil hijrah. Kalendar Islam bermula dari tahun ia berlaku!",
 "Ketua-ketua Makkah membuat rancangan jahat untuk menyerang Nabi ﷺ pada waktu malam. Allah memberitahu baginda tentang rancangan itu. Kitab-kitab sirah menceritakan bahawa Saidina Ali tidur di katil baginda pada malam itu, manakala Nabi ﷺ keluar dengan selamat.",
 "Baginda dan sahabat baiknya, Saidina Abu Bakar, tidak pergi ke utara menuju Madinah. Mereka pergi ke selatan, arah yang bertentangan, ke bukit ini, Thur. Mereka bersembunyi di dalam sebuah gua kecil berhampiran puncaknya. Bijak, bukan?",
 "Kaum Quraisy sangat marah. Mereka menjanjikan 100 ekor unta kepada sesiapa yang dapat menangkap mereka. Orang yang mencari mereka mendaki sampai ke atas, betul-betul di mulut gua! Abu Bakar dapat melihat kaki mereka. Dia berbisik: “Kalau salah seorang daripada mereka melihat ke bawah kakinya, tentu dia nampak kita!”",
 "Nabi ﷺ menjawab dengan tenang: “Apa pendapatmu tentang dua orang, yang Allah ialah yang ketiga bersama mereka?” (Bukhari, Muslim) Allah menceritakan kisah ini dalam al-Quran: “Janganlah engkau berdukacita, sesungguhnya Allah bersama kita.” (At-Taubah 9:40) Orang-orang yang mencari itu pun berpatah balik dan pergi.",
 "Mungkin kamu pernah dengar bahawa seekor labah-labah membuat sarang di mulut gua, jadi orang yang mencari itu menyangka tiada sesiapa yang masuk ke dalam. Kisah ini ada dalam Musnad Ahmad. Sebahagian ulama, seperti Ibnu Kathir dan Ibnu Hajar, mengatakan ia hasan (baik), dan ulama lain mengatakan sanadnya lemah. Kisah dua ekor burung merpati yang bersarang di pintu gua lebih lemah lagi.",
 "Satu lagi kisah yang selalu diceritakan: Abu Bakar masuk dahulu dan menutup lubang-lubang di dalam gua dengan cebisan kainnya. Nabi ﷺ tertidur dengan kepala baginda di atas riba Abu Bakar. Seekor ular mematuk kaki Abu Bakar dari lubang yang terakhir, tetapi dia tidak bergerak, supaya tidak mengejutkan sahabatnya. Air matanya jatuh ke wajah Nabi ﷺ. Nabi ﷺ terjaga, menyapu sedikit air liur baginda pada tempat patukan itu, dan sakitnya pun hilang. Ulama mengatakan sanad kisah ini lemah, jadi kita menceritakannya sebagai kisah, bukan sebagai perkara yang pasti. Yang kita tahu dengan pasti, daripada al-Quran dan Bukhari, ialah Allah menjaga mereka dengan selamat.",
 "Mereka tinggal di dalam gua itu selama 3 malam. Setiap petang, anak Abu Bakar, Abdullah, datang diam-diam untuk memberitahu mereka berita dari Makkah. Seorang penggembala, Amir bin Fuhairah, membawa kambing-kambingnya lalu di depan gua supaya mereka boleh minum susu segar, dan kuku kambing-kambing itu menutup kesan tapak kaki mereka! (Bukhari)",
 "Anak perempuan Abu Bakar, Asma', membawa makanan untuk perjalanan mereka. Dia tiada apa-apa untuk mengikat beg itu, jadi dia mengoyakkan tali pinggangnya kepada dua dan menggunakan separuh daripadanya. Selepas itu dia digelar “pemilik dua tali pinggang”. (Bukhari)",
 "Selepas 3 hari, apabila pencarian sudah reda, seorang penunjuk jalan membawa unta, dan mereka bertolak ke Madinah melalui jalan rahsia di sepanjang pantai.",
 "Bukit ini sangat tinggi dan sukar didaki, jadi kebanyakan orang melihatnya dari bawah sahaja."],
 look:["Puncaknya yang tinggi dan berbatu. Cuba bayangkan mendakinya pada waktu malam, tanpa jalan.","Betapa jauhnya Thur dari Kaabah. Mereka pergi ke arah yang bertentangan dengan Madinah!"],
 think:"Abu Bakar berasa takut, tetapi Nabi ﷺ mengingatkannya bahawa Allah bersama mereka. Apabila kamu berasa takut, apa yang boleh kamu katakan kepada diri sendiri?"}},

"Arafah and Jabal Rahmah":{img:["arafah","arafah-crowd"],
 en:{cap:["Jabal Rahmah, the Mountain of Mercy, with its white pillar on top.","On the Day of Arafah, pilgrims in white fill the whole plain."],
 p:["Arafah is a huge, flat plain outside Makkah. In it is a small rocky hill called Jabal Rahmah, the Mountain of Mercy.",
 "For most of the year it is very quiet. But on one day each year, the 9th of Dhul Hijjah, about 2 million pilgrims stand here together in white, praying and asking Allah for forgiveness.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ said: “Hajj is Arafah.” It is the most important part of Hajj. If a pilgrim misses Arafah, they miss Hajj.",
 "In the year 10 AH, the Prophet ﷺ made his only Hajj, called the Farewell Hajj. He stood by the big rocks at the bottom of Jabal Rahmah, on his camel Al-Qaswa', raising his hands in dua from the afternoon until the sun set. (Muslim)",
 "On that day, Allah revealed: “Today I have perfected your religion for you.” (Al-Ma'idah 5:3)",
 "The Prophet ﷺ said that there is no day on which Allah frees more people from the Fire than the Day of Arafah. (Muslim) That is why the dua on this day is so special.",
 "Even people who are not at Hajj can join in. Many Muslims around the world fast on the Day of Arafah.",
 "You might see lots of green trees on the plain. In Indonesia, people call them “Soekarno trees”, after the Indonesian president who suggested planting them to give pilgrims shade.",
 "Climbing Jabal Rahmah is not part of Umrah or Hajj, and there is no special reward for it. The whole plain of Arafah is the place of standing."],
 look:["The white pillar on top of Jabal Rahmah.","The big rocks at the bottom, near where the Prophet ﷺ stood.","Signboards showing where Arafah starts and ends."],
 think:"On the Day of Arafah, people ask Allah for everything they need. If you could ask Allah for 3 things, what would they be?"},
 ms:{cap:["Jabal Rahmah, Bukit Rahmat, dengan tiang putih di puncaknya.","Pada Hari Arafah, jemaah berpakaian putih memenuhi seluruh padang."],
 p:["Arafah ialah padang yang sangat luas dan rata di luar Makkah. Di situ ada sebuah bukit kecil berbatu bernama Jabal Rahmah, Bukit Rahmat.",
 "Hampir sepanjang tahun, tempat ini sangat sunyi. Tetapi pada satu hari setiap tahun, iaitu 9 Zulhijjah, kira-kira 2 juta jemaah berwukuf di sini bersama-sama dengan pakaian putih, berdoa dan memohon keampunan Allah.",
 "Nabi ﷺ bersabda: “Haji itu ialah Arafah.” Ia bahagian yang paling penting dalam ibadah haji. Jika seorang jemaah terlepas Arafah, dia terlepas hajinya.",
 "Pada tahun 10 H, Nabi ﷺ menunaikan satu-satunya haji baginda, yang dipanggil Haji Wada'. Baginda berwukuf di tepi batu-batu besar di kaki Jabal Rahmah, di atas untanya Al-Qaswa', sambil mengangkat tangan berdoa dari waktu petang hingga matahari terbenam. (Muslim)",
 "Pada hari itu, Allah menurunkan ayat: “Pada hari ini, Aku telah sempurnakan bagi kamu agama kamu.” (Al-Ma'idah 5:3)",
 "Nabi ﷺ bersabda bahawa tiada hari yang Allah membebaskan lebih ramai manusia daripada api neraka selain Hari Arafah. (Muslim) Sebab itulah doa pada hari ini sangat istimewa.",
 "Orang yang tidak menunaikan haji pun boleh turut serta. Ramai umat Islam di seluruh dunia berpuasa pada Hari Arafah.",
 "Kamu mungkin nampak banyak pokok hijau di padang ini. Di Indonesia, orang memanggilnya “pokok Soekarno”, sempena nama presiden Indonesia yang mencadangkan supaya pokok-pokok itu ditanam untuk memberi teduhan kepada jemaah.",
 "Mendaki Jabal Rahmah bukan sebahagian daripada umrah atau haji, dan tiada pahala istimewa untuknya. Seluruh padang Arafah ialah tempat wukuf."],
 look:["Tiang putih di puncak Jabal Rahmah.","Batu-batu besar di kaki bukit, dekat tempat Nabi ﷺ berwukuf.","Papan tanda yang menunjukkan di mana Arafah bermula dan berakhir."],
 think:"Pada Hari Arafah, orang ramai memohon kepada Allah segala yang mereka perlukan. Jika kamu boleh meminta 3 perkara daripada Allah, apakah perkara itu?"}},

"Masjid Namirah":{img:["namirah"],
 en:{cap:["Masjid Namirah at sunset, at the edge of Arafah."],
 p:["Masjid Namirah is one of the biggest mosques in the area. It stands at the edge of Arafah and can hold hundreds of thousands of people.",
 "On his Farewell Hajj, the Prophet ﷺ rested in a tent at Namirah. After midday, he rode into the valley of 'Uranah, right next to where the mosque is now, and gave a famous speech. It is called the Farewell Sermon. (Muslim)",
 "He told everyone: “Your lives and your belongings are sacred, as sacred as this day, in this month, in this town.” That means: never hurt another person, and never take what belongs to someone else.",
 "He told the men to fear Allah in how they treat women, and to be good to them.",
 "He said: “I am leaving you something. If you hold on to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah.”",
 "Then he asked the huge crowd: “You will be asked about me. What will you say?” They answered: “We bear witness that you delivered the message and did your duty.” He raised his finger to the sky, then pointed at the people, and said: “O Allah, be witness. O Allah, be witness.” 3 times. (Muslim)",
 "Every year on the Day of Arafah, a sermon is given at this mosque, and pilgrims pray Zuhr and Asr together here, just as the Prophet ﷺ did.",
 "Here is a fun fact: the front part of the mosque is outside Arafah, and the back part is inside. Signs inside the mosque show where the line is."],
 look:["The tall minarets, which you can see from far away.","If you go inside, the signs that mark the edge of Arafah."],
 think:"The Prophet ﷺ said everyone's life and belongings are precious. How can you take care of other people's things?"},
 ms:{cap:["Masjid Namirah ketika matahari terbenam, di pinggir Arafah."],
 p:["Masjid Namirah ialah salah sebuah masjid yang terbesar di kawasan ini. Ia terletak di pinggir Arafah dan boleh memuatkan ratusan ribu orang.",
 "Semasa Haji Wada', Nabi ﷺ berehat di dalam khemah di Namirah. Selepas tengah hari, baginda pergi dengan tunggangannya ke lembah 'Uranah, betul-betul di sebelah tempat masjid itu sekarang, dan menyampaikan ucapan yang terkenal. Ia dipanggil Khutbah Wada'. (Muslim)",
 "Baginda memberitahu semua orang: “Nyawa kamu dan harta kamu adalah suci, sesuci hari ini, dalam bulan ini, di negeri ini.” Maksudnya: jangan sekali-kali menyakiti orang lain, dan jangan sekali-kali mengambil barang milik orang lain.",
 "Baginda menyuruh kaum lelaki bertakwa kepada Allah dalam cara mereka melayan wanita, dan berbuat baik kepada mereka.",
 "Baginda bersabda: “Aku tinggalkan untuk kamu sesuatu. Jika kamu berpegang teguh padanya, kamu tidak akan sesat selama-lamanya: Kitab Allah.”",
 "Kemudian baginda bertanya kepada orang ramai yang sangat besar itu: “Kamu akan ditanya tentang aku. Apa yang akan kamu katakan?” Mereka menjawab: “Kami bersaksi bahawa engkau telah menyampaikan risalah dan telah menunaikan tugasmu.” Baginda mengangkat jari ke langit, kemudian menunjuk ke arah orang ramai, dan bersabda: “Ya Allah, saksikanlah. Ya Allah, saksikanlah.” 3 kali. (Muslim)",
 "Setiap tahun pada Hari Arafah, khutbah disampaikan di masjid ini, dan jemaah solat Zuhur dan Asar bersama-sama di sini, sama seperti yang dilakukan oleh Nabi ﷺ.",
 "Ini satu fakta menarik: bahagian depan masjid berada di luar Arafah, dan bahagian belakangnya di dalam Arafah. Papan tanda di dalam masjid menunjukkan di mana garis sempadannya."],
 look:["Menara-menaranya yang tinggi, yang boleh dilihat dari jauh.","Jika kamu masuk ke dalam, papan tanda yang menandakan sempadan Arafah."],
 think:"Nabi ﷺ bersabda bahawa nyawa dan harta setiap orang sangat berharga. Bagaimana kamu boleh menjaga barang milik orang lain?"}},

"Muzdalifah":{img:["muzdalifah"],
 en:{cap:["Fajr in Muzdalifah. Pilgrims slept here under the open sky."],
 p:["Muzdalifah is an open plain between Arafah and Mina. During Hajj, after the sun sets on the Day of Arafah, millions of pilgrims leave Arafah and come here.",
 "On his Hajj, the Prophet ﷺ arrived here and prayed Maghrib and Isha together. Then he lay down and slept until dawn. (Muslim)",
 "So pilgrims sleep here too, on mats, under the stars. It is like a giant camp-out with millions of people! Rich or poor, everyone sleeps on the ground.",
 "After Fajr, the Prophet ﷺ went to a place called Al-Mash'ar Al-Haram. He faced the qiblah and made dua, saying Allahu Akbar and La ilaha illallah, until the sky was bright. He left before sunrise. (Muslim) Allah mentions this place in the Quran (Al-Baqarah 2:198). There is a mosque there today.",
 "Many pilgrims pick up small pebbles here, about the size of a chickpea, to throw at the Jamarat in Mina the next day.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ was kind to people who were old or weak. He let his wife Sawdah, who found it hard to move in crowds, leave earlier in the night, before the big rush. (Bukhari)"],
 look:["The wide, empty plain with tall lamp posts.","Masjid Al-Mash'ar Al-Haram.","Signboards showing where Muzdalifah starts and ends."],
 think:"At Muzdalifah, kings and workers sleep on the same ground. Why do you think Allah made everyone equal here?"},
 ms:{cap:["Waktu Subuh di Muzdalifah. Jemaah tidur di sini di bawah langit terbuka."],
 p:["Muzdalifah ialah padang terbuka di antara Arafah dan Mina. Semasa musim haji, selepas matahari terbenam pada Hari Arafah, berjuta-juta jemaah meninggalkan Arafah dan datang ke sini.",
 "Semasa haji baginda, Nabi ﷺ tiba di sini lalu solat Maghrib dan Isyak bersama-sama. Kemudian baginda berbaring dan tidur hingga waktu fajar. (Muslim)",
 "Jadi jemaah pun tidur di sini, di atas tikar, di bawah bintang-bintang. Ia seperti perkhemahan gergasi dengan berjuta-juta orang! Kaya atau miskin, semua orang tidur di atas tanah.",
 "Selepas Subuh, Nabi ﷺ pergi ke tempat bernama Al-Masy'aril Haram. Baginda menghadap kiblat dan berdoa, sambil menyebut Allahu Akbar dan La ilaha illallah, sehingga langit menjadi terang. Baginda bertolak sebelum matahari terbit. (Muslim) Allah menyebut tempat ini dalam al-Quran (Al-Baqarah 2:198). Hari ini ada sebuah masjid di situ.",
 "Ramai jemaah mengutip batu-batu kecil di sini, kira-kira sebesar kacang kuda, untuk dilontar ke Jamarat di Mina keesokan harinya.",
 "Nabi ﷺ bersikap baik kepada orang yang tua atau lemah. Baginda membenarkan isterinya, Saudah, yang sukar bergerak dalam orang ramai, bertolak lebih awal pada waktu malam, sebelum orang ramai berasak-asak. (Bukhari)"],
 look:["Padang yang luas dan kosong dengan tiang-tiang lampu yang tinggi.","Masjid Al-Masy'aril Haram.","Papan tanda yang menunjukkan di mana Muzdalifah bermula dan berakhir."],
 think:"Di Muzdalifah, raja dan pekerja tidur di atas tanah yang sama. Pada pendapat kamu, mengapa Allah menjadikan semua orang sama di sini?"}},

"Jamarat and Masjid Khaif, Mina":{img:["jamarat","mina"],
 en:{cap:["One of the Jamarat walls, inside the big Jamarat building.","Mina's white tents. During Hajj, millions of pilgrims stay here."],
 p:["Mina is a valley between Makkah and Muzdalifah. During Hajj it turns into a city of white tents, all in neat rows, with cool air blowing inside.",
 "In Mina there are 3 places called the Jamarat. Today they are tall walls inside a huge building with many floors, so millions of people can throw pebbles safely.",
 "Why do pilgrims throw pebbles here? Ibn Abbas, a Companion, told this story: when Prophet Ibrahim came here, Shaytan appeared and tried to stop him from obeying Allah. Ibrahim threw 7 small stones at him, and Shaytan went away. It happened at all 3 places.",
 "What was Ibrahim doing? Allah was testing him. In a dream, Allah told him to sacrifice his dear son Ismail.",
 "Ibrahim told Ismail about the dream. Ismail said: “O my father, do what you are commanded. You will find me, if Allah wills, one of the patient.” (As-Saffat 37:102)",
 "Just as Ibrahim was about to do it, Allah stopped him and sent a ram instead. Father and son had both passed the test! (As-Saffat 37:103–107) That is why Muslims sacrifice an animal on Eid al-Adha and share the meat with family, friends and the poor.",
 "When pilgrims throw the pebbles, they say “Allahu Akbar” each time. They are following the Prophet ﷺ and showing that, like Ibrahim, they will say no to Shaytan.",
 "Masjid Khaif is the big mosque of Mina. The Prophet ﷺ prayed here during his Hajj."],
 look:["The Jamarat building with its many floors and ramps.","The tents with pointed roofs.","Masjid Khaif and its minarets."],
 think:"Ibrahim said no to Shaytan 3 times. When something inside you says “do the wrong thing”, what could you do?"},
 ms:{cap:["Salah satu dinding Jamarat, di dalam bangunan Jamarat yang besar.","Khemah-khemah putih di Mina. Semasa musim haji, berjuta-juta jemaah tinggal di sini."],
 p:["Mina ialah sebuah lembah di antara Makkah dan Muzdalifah. Semasa musim haji, ia bertukar menjadi bandar khemah putih, tersusun dalam barisan yang kemas, dengan udara sejuk bertiup di dalamnya.",
 "Di Mina ada 3 tempat yang dipanggil Jamarat. Hari ini, ia ialah dinding-dinding tinggi di dalam sebuah bangunan besar yang mempunyai banyak tingkat, supaya berjuta-juta orang boleh melontar batu dengan selamat.",
 "Mengapa jemaah melontar batu di sini? Ibnu Abbas, seorang sahabat, menceritakan kisah ini: apabila Nabi Ibrahim datang ke sini, syaitan muncul dan cuba menghalangnya daripada mentaati Allah. Nabi Ibrahim melontar 7 biji batu kecil kepadanya, lalu syaitan pun pergi. Perkara ini berlaku di ketiga-tiga tempat.",
 "Apakah yang sedang Nabi Ibrahim lakukan? Allah sedang mengujinya. Dalam mimpi, Allah menyuruhnya menyembelih anak kesayangannya, Nabi Ismail.",
 "Nabi Ibrahim memberitahu Nabi Ismail tentang mimpi itu. Nabi Ismail berkata: “Wahai ayahku, lakukanlah apa yang diperintahkan kepadamu. Insya-Allah, engkau akan mendapati aku termasuk orang-orang yang sabar.” (As-Saffat 37:102)",
 "Ketika Nabi Ibrahim hampir melakukannya, Allah menghentikannya dan menghantar seekor kibas sebagai ganti. Ayah dan anak itu kedua-duanya lulus ujian! (As-Saffat 37:103–107) Sebab itulah umat Islam menyembelih haiwan korban pada Hari Raya Aidiladha dan berkongsi dagingnya dengan keluarga, kawan-kawan dan orang miskin.",
 "Apabila jemaah melontar batu, mereka menyebut “Allahu Akbar” setiap kali. Mereka mengikut Nabi ﷺ dan menunjukkan bahawa, seperti Nabi Ibrahim, mereka akan berkata tidak kepada syaitan.",
 "Masjid Khaif ialah masjid besar di Mina. Nabi ﷺ solat di sini semasa haji baginda."],
 look:["Bangunan Jamarat dengan banyak tingkat dan tanjakannya.","Khemah-khemah dengan bumbung yang tirus.","Masjid Khaif dan menara-menaranya."],
 think:"Nabi Ibrahim berkata tidak kepada syaitan 3 kali. Apabila ada sesuatu dalam hati kamu yang berkata “buatlah perkara yang salah”, apa yang boleh kamu lakukan?"}},

"The journey to Taif":{img:["taif"],
 en:{cap:["The winding road up the mountains to Taif."],
 p:["Taif is a city high up in the mountains, about 2 hours by road from Makkah. It is much cooler up here! Taif is famous for its fruit, its honey, and its pink roses that are made into rose water.",
 "In the 10th year after he became a prophet, the Prophet ﷺ had a very sad year. His wife Khadijah died, and so did his uncle Abu Talib, who had always protected him. After that, the people of Makkah hurt him even more.",
 "So he walked all the way to Taif with Zayd ibn Harithah, to invite its people to worship Allah. He hoped they would listen.",
 "But the leaders of Taif were rude. They laughed at him and told the boys and servants to throw stones at him and chase him out of town. His feet were hurt and bleeding.",
 "Tired and hurt, he rested in a garden. The seerah books tell that the garden's owners sent their servant, a Christian man named Addas, with a plate of grapes. The Prophet ﷺ said “Bismillah” before eating. Addas was surprised: people here never said that! The Prophet ﷺ asked where he was from. “Nineveh,” said Addas. “The town of the good man Yunus,” said the Prophet ﷺ. “He was a prophet, and so am I.” Addas kissed his head and hands.",
 "On the way back, Jibril came with the Angel of the Mountains. The angel said: “If you want, I will bring the two mountains down on them.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "But the Prophet ﷺ said no. He said: “I hope Allah will bring from their children people who worship Allah alone.”",
 "His hope came true. A few years later, the people of Taif became Muslim.",
 "Later, Aisyah asked him if he had ever had a day harder than the Battle of Uhud. He told her about this day. (Bukhari)"],
 look:["The twisty road up the mountain.","Rose farms, and shops selling rose water.","Baboons by the roadside! Look, but don't feed them or go near."],
 think:"When people were mean to him, the Prophet ﷺ didn't wish them harm. He hoped for good. Can you be kind to someone who wasn't kind to you?"},
 ms:{cap:["Jalan berliku-liku mendaki gunung ke Taif."],
 p:["Taif ialah sebuah bandar yang terletak tinggi di atas gunung, kira-kira 2 jam perjalanan dari Makkah. Cuacanya jauh lebih sejuk di sini! Taif terkenal dengan buah-buahannya, madunya, dan bunga mawar merah jambunya yang dijadikan air mawar.",
 "Pada tahun ke-10 selepas baginda menjadi nabi, Nabi ﷺ melalui tahun yang sangat menyedihkan. Isteri baginda, Khadijah, wafat, begitu juga bapa saudara baginda, Abu Talib, yang selama ini melindungi baginda. Selepas itu, penduduk Makkah lebih menyakiti baginda.",
 "Jadi baginda berjalan kaki jauh ke Taif bersama Zaid bin Harithah, untuk mengajak penduduknya menyembah Allah. Baginda berharap mereka akan mendengar.",
 "Tetapi ketua-ketua Taif bersikap kurang ajar. Mereka mentertawakan baginda dan menyuruh budak-budak dan hamba-hamba melempar batu kepada baginda dan menghalau baginda keluar dari bandar. Kaki baginda cedera dan berdarah.",
 "Dalam keadaan letih dan cedera, baginda berehat di sebuah kebun. Kitab-kitab sirah menceritakan bahawa pemilik kebun itu menghantar hamba mereka, seorang lelaki Kristian bernama Addas, dengan sepinggan anggur. Nabi ﷺ menyebut “Bismillah” sebelum makan. Addas terkejut: orang di sini tidak pernah menyebutnya! Nabi ﷺ bertanya dari mana asalnya. “Nineveh,” jawab Addas. “Negeri lelaki soleh, Yunus,” kata Nabi ﷺ. “Dia seorang nabi, dan aku juga seorang nabi.” Addas mencium kepala dan tangan baginda.",
 "Dalam perjalanan pulang, Jibril datang bersama Malaikat Penjaga Gunung. Malaikat itu berkata: “Jika engkau mahu, aku akan hempapkan dua gunung itu ke atas mereka.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Tetapi Nabi ﷺ berkata tidak. Baginda bersabda: “Aku berharap Allah akan melahirkan daripada anak-anak mereka orang yang menyembah Allah sahaja.”",
 "Harapan baginda menjadi kenyataan. Beberapa tahun kemudian, penduduk Taif memeluk Islam.",
 "Kemudian, Aisyah bertanya kepada baginda sama ada baginda pernah melalui hari yang lebih sukar daripada hari Perang Uhud. Baginda menceritakan kepadanya tentang hari ini. (Bukhari)"],
 look:["Jalan yang berliku-liku mendaki gunung.","Ladang mawar, dan kedai yang menjual air mawar.","Babun di tepi jalan! Tengok sahaja, tetapi jangan beri makan atau pergi dekat."],
 think:"Apabila orang berlaku jahat kepada baginda, Nabi ﷺ tidak mendoakan keburukan untuk mereka. Baginda mengharapkan kebaikan. Bolehkah kamu berbuat baik kepada seseorang yang tidak berbuat baik kepada kamu?"}},

"Masjid Abdullah ibn Abbas":{img:["ibn-abbas"],
 en:{cap:["Masjid Abdullah ibn Abbas in Taif."],
 p:["This mosque in Taif is named after Abdullah ibn Abbas, the Prophet's ﷺ young cousin. His father, Al-Abbas, was the Prophet's ﷺ uncle.",
 "Ibn Abbas was just a boy while the Prophet ﷺ was alive. He was only about 13 when the Prophet ﷺ passed away. So he was a kid, just like you!",
 "One night, young Ibn Abbas put out water for the Prophet ﷺ to make wudu. The Prophet ﷺ asked who had done it. When he found out, he made a dua for him: “O Allah, give him deep understanding of the religion.” (Bukhari)",
 "Once, while riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, Ibn Abbas heard him say: “Young boy, I will teach you some words. Be mindful of Allah, and He will protect you. Be mindful of Allah, and you will find Him in front of you. When you ask, ask Allah. When you need help, ask Allah for help.” (Tirmidhi)",
 "Allah answered the Prophet's ﷺ dua. Ibn Abbas grew up loving to learn. After the Prophet ﷺ died, he went to the older Companions to learn the hadith they knew. Sometimes he waited outside a Companion's door while he napped, resting his head on his cloak as the wind blew dust on his face, so he would not wake him up!",
 "He became one of the greatest teachers of the Quran. People called him “the ocean” because his knowledge was so deep.",
 "When he grew old, he lost his eyesight. He moved to Taif, and he died and was buried here, next to this mosque."],
 look:["The old stone mosque and its minaret.","The quiet graveyard area beside it."],
 think:"Ibn Abbas was a child when he learned: “Be mindful of Allah, and He will protect you.” Can you learn it by heart today?"},
 ms:{cap:["Masjid Abdullah bin Abbas di Taif."],
 p:["Masjid di Taif ini dinamakan sempena Abdullah bin Abbas, sepupu muda Nabi ﷺ. Bapanya, Al-Abbas, ialah bapa saudara Nabi ﷺ.",
 "Ibnu Abbas masih kanak-kanak semasa Nabi ﷺ masih hidup. Umurnya baru kira-kira 13 tahun ketika Nabi ﷺ wafat. Jadi dia seorang budak, sama seperti kamu!",
 "Pada suatu malam, Ibnu Abbas yang masih kecil menyediakan air untuk Nabi ﷺ mengambil wuduk. Nabi ﷺ bertanya siapa yang melakukannya. Apabila baginda tahu, baginda mendoakannya: “Ya Allah, berikanlah dia kefahaman yang mendalam tentang agama.” (Bukhari)",
 "Pada suatu hari, ketika membonceng di belakang Nabi ﷺ, Ibnu Abbas mendengar baginda bersabda: “Wahai anak, aku akan ajarkan kepadamu beberapa kalimah. Jagalah Allah, nescaya Allah akan menjagamu. Jagalah Allah, nescaya kamu akan dapati Dia di hadapanmu. Apabila kamu meminta, mintalah kepada Allah. Apabila kamu memerlukan pertolongan, mohonlah pertolongan kepada Allah.” (Tirmidhi)",
 "Allah memakbulkan doa Nabi ﷺ. Ibnu Abbas membesar dengan sangat suka belajar. Selepas Nabi ﷺ wafat, dia pergi berjumpa sahabat-sahabat yang lebih tua untuk mempelajari hadis yang mereka tahu. Kadang-kadang dia menunggu di luar pintu rumah seorang sahabat yang sedang tidur sebentar, berbantalkan kainnya sambil angin meniup debu ke mukanya, supaya dia tidak mengejutkan sahabat itu!",
 "Dia menjadi salah seorang guru al-Quran yang paling hebat. Orang memanggilnya “lautan” kerana ilmunya sangat dalam.",
 "Apabila sudah tua, dia hilang penglihatan. Dia berpindah ke Taif, lalu meninggal dunia dan dikebumikan di sini, di sebelah masjid ini."],
 look:["Masjid batu yang lama dan menaranya.","Kawasan perkuburan yang tenang di sebelahnya."],
 think:"Ibnu Abbas masih kanak-kanak ketika dia belajar: “Jagalah Allah, nescaya Allah akan menjagamu.” Bolehkah kamu menghafalnya hari ini?"}},

"Masjid An-Nabawi":{img:["nabawi","umbrellas"],
 en:{cap:["The Green Dome of Masjid An-Nabawi in Madinah.","Giant umbrellas open in the courtyard to give shade."],
 p:["When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah after the Hijrah, everyone wanted him to stay at their house! People held his camel's reins and begged him. The seerah books tell that he said: “Let her go, she is following Allah's command.”",
 "The camel walked on, then knelt down on a piece of land used for drying dates. It belonged to two orphan boys, Sahl and Suhayl. They wanted to give it as a gift, but the Prophet ﷺ paid for it. (Bukhari)",
 "Then everyone built the masjid together. The walls were mud bricks, the pillars were palm tree trunks, and the roof was palm leaves. The Prophet ﷺ carried bricks himself, just like everyone else. (Bukhari)",
 "The Prophet ﷺ used to lean on a palm trunk when he gave his talk on Fridays. When the people made him a minbar with steps, he moved to it. Then the palm trunk began to cry, like a little child! The Prophet ﷺ came down and hugged it, until it went quiet. (Bukhari)",
 "Some poor Companions with no homes lived on a shaded platform at the back of the masjid, called the Suffah. Abu Hurairah was one of them. He stayed close to the Prophet ﷺ and learned more hadith than almost anyone.",
 "Today the masjid is many, many times bigger than the first one. Giant umbrellas in the courtyard open in the morning to give shade.",
 "Under the Green Dome is the room of Aisyah, where the Prophet ﷺ is buried. Abu Bakr and Umar are buried beside him.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ said that one prayer in his masjid is better than 1,000 prayers anywhere else, except Masjid Al-Haram. (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "When you walk past his grave, you can say: “Assalamu 'alaika ya Rasulallah”: peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."],
 look:["The Green Dome.","The giant umbrellas. Watch them open or close!","Domes in the roof that slide open to the sky.","The numbered gates. Remember yours so you don't get lost."],
 think:"The Prophet ﷺ was the leader, but he still carried bricks. How can you help when your family is busy?"},
 ms:{cap:["Kubah Hijau Masjid Nabawi di Madinah.","Payung-payung gergasi terbuka di halaman untuk memberi teduhan."],
 p:["Apabila Nabi ﷺ tiba di Madinah selepas hijrah, semua orang mahu baginda tinggal di rumah mereka! Orang ramai memegang tali unta baginda dan merayu kepada baginda. Kitab-kitab sirah menceritakan bahawa baginda bersabda: “Biarkan unta ini, ia mengikut perintah Allah.”",
 "Unta itu terus berjalan, kemudian duduk melutut di sebidang tanah yang digunakan untuk menjemur kurma. Tanah itu milik dua orang budak yatim, Sahl dan Suhail. Mereka mahu memberikannya sebagai hadiah, tetapi Nabi ﷺ membayarnya. (Bukhari)",
 "Kemudian semua orang membina masjid itu bersama-sama. Dindingnya daripada bata lumpur, tiangnya daripada batang pokok kurma, dan bumbungnya daripada daun kurma. Nabi ﷺ sendiri mengangkat bata, sama seperti orang lain. (Bukhari)",
 "Nabi ﷺ biasanya bersandar pada sebatang pokok kurma ketika menyampaikan khutbah pada hari Jumaat. Apabila orang ramai membuatkan baginda sebuah mimbar bertangga, baginda berpindah ke mimbar itu. Lalu batang pokok kurma itu mula menangis, seperti budak kecil! Nabi ﷺ turun dan memeluknya, sehingga ia diam. (Bukhari)",
 "Sebilangan sahabat miskin yang tiada rumah tinggal di sebuah serambi berbumbung di bahagian belakang masjid, dipanggil Suffah. Abu Hurairah ialah salah seorang daripada mereka. Dia sentiasa dekat dengan Nabi ﷺ dan mempelajari lebih banyak hadis daripada hampir semua orang lain.",
 "Hari ini, masjid ini berkali-kali ganda lebih besar daripada masjid yang pertama. Payung-payung gergasi di halaman terbuka pada waktu pagi untuk memberi teduhan.",
 "Di bawah Kubah Hijau ialah bilik Aisyah, tempat Nabi ﷺ dimakamkan. Saidina Abu Bakar dan Umar dimakamkan di sebelah baginda.",
 "Nabi ﷺ bersabda bahawa satu solat di masjid baginda lebih baik daripada 1,000 solat di tempat lain, kecuali Masjidil Haram. (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Apabila kamu melalui makam baginda, kamu boleh mengucapkan: “Assalamu 'alaika ya Rasulallah”: salam sejahtera ke atasmu, wahai Rasulullah."],
 look:["Kubah Hijau.","Payung-payung gergasi. Tengok ia terbuka atau tertutup!","Kubah di bumbung yang boleh bergerak terbuka ke langit.","Pintu-pintu yang bernombor. Ingat nombor pintu kamu supaya tidak sesat."],
 think:"Nabi ﷺ seorang pemimpin, tetapi baginda tetap mengangkat bata. Bagaimana kamu boleh membantu apabila keluarga kamu sibuk?"}},

"The Rawdah":{img:["green-dome"],
 en:{cap:["The Green Dome. The Rawdah is inside, right next to it."],
 p:["Inside Masjid An-Nabawi there is a special place, between where the Prophet's ﷺ house was and his minbar. He said: “Between my house and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Rawdah means “garden”. You can spot it by its green carpet. Most of the rest of the masjid has red carpet.",
 "It is quite small, and everyone wants to pray there. So you need a permit from the Nusuk app and a time slot, and you go in with a group.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ also said: “My minbar is on my Pond.” (Bukhari) The Pond, Al-Hawd, is in the Hereafter, where he will give his people a drink, and whoever drinks from it will never be thirsty again.",
 "Look at the white pillars. Some have names. One is the Pillar of Repentance. The seerah books tell that a Companion named Abu Lubabah made a mistake and felt so sorry that he tied himself to this pillar until Allah forgave him.",
 "When it's your turn, pray 2 rakaat calmly and make dua. Then leave room for others. Don't push. Being gentle is part of the reward."],
 look:["The green carpet.","The Prophet's ﷺ minbar.","The white pillars with name signs."],
 think:"If you had a few minutes in a garden of Paradise, what dua would you make?"},
 ms:{cap:["Kubah Hijau. Raudhah berada di dalam, betul-betul di sebelahnya."],
 p:["Di dalam Masjid Nabawi ada satu tempat istimewa, di antara tempat rumah Nabi ﷺ dahulu dan mimbar baginda. Baginda bersabda: “Antara rumahku dan mimbarku ialah sebuah taman daripada taman-taman syurga.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Raudhah bermaksud “taman”. Kamu boleh mengenalinya melalui permaidaninya yang berwarna hijau. Kebanyakan bahagian lain masjid ini berpermaidani merah.",
 "Tempatnya agak kecil, dan semua orang mahu solat di situ. Jadi kamu perlukan permit daripada aplikasi Nusuk dan slot masa, dan kamu masuk bersama satu kumpulan.",
 "Nabi ﷺ juga bersabda: “Mimbarku berada di atas Telagaku.” (Bukhari) Telaga itu, Al-Haudh, berada di akhirat, tempat baginda akan memberi umatnya minum, dan sesiapa yang minum daripadanya tidak akan dahaga lagi selama-lamanya.",
 "Lihatlah tiang-tiang putih itu. Ada yang mempunyai nama. Salah satunya ialah Tiang Taubat. Kitab-kitab sirah menceritakan bahawa seorang sahabat bernama Abu Lubabah melakukan kesilapan dan berasa sangat menyesal sehingga dia mengikat dirinya pada tiang ini sehingga Allah mengampunkannya.",
 "Apabila tiba giliran kamu, solatlah 2 rakaat dengan tenang dan berdoalah. Kemudian berilah ruang kepada orang lain. Jangan menolak. Bersikap lembut juga sebahagian daripada pahalanya."],
 look:["Permaidani hijau.","Mimbar Nabi ﷺ.","Tiang-tiang putih dengan papan nama."],
 think:"Jika kamu ada beberapa minit di sebuah taman syurga, apakah doa yang akan kamu baca?"}},

"Masjid Quba'":{img:["quba"],
 en:{cap:["Masjid Quba', the first masjid in Islam."],
 p:["Quba' was a village just outside Madinah. When the Muslims of Madinah heard the Prophet ﷺ had left Makkah, they walked out every morning to wait for him, until the sun got too hot.",
 "One day, a man standing high on a lookout shouted: “He's here! The one you're waiting for is here!” Everyone rushed out to welcome him. (Bukhari)",
 "The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Quba' for a few days, and he built the very first masjid in Islam here. He carried stones with his own hands.",
 "Allah praised this masjid in the Quran: “a masjid founded on piety from the very first day... In it are people who love to keep themselves clean and pure.” (At-Tawbah 9:108)",
 "Even after he moved into the city, the Prophet ﷺ loved to visit Quba' every Saturday, sometimes walking and sometimes riding, and pray 2 rakaat. (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "He said that whoever makes wudu at home, then comes to Masjid Quba' and prays in it, gets a reward like an Umrah. (Ibn Majah, An-Nasa'i) So make wudu at the hotel before you go!"],
 look:["The white domes and the tall white minarets.","The cool, open courtyard."],
 think:"A reward like a whole Umrah, for wudu and a short visit! Allah gives so much for small good deeds. What small good deed can you do today?"},
 ms:{cap:["Masjid Quba', masjid pertama dalam Islam."],
 p:["Quba' dahulunya sebuah kampung di luar Madinah. Apabila orang Islam di Madinah mendengar bahawa Nabi ﷺ telah meninggalkan Makkah, mereka keluar setiap pagi untuk menunggu baginda, sehingga matahari menjadi terlalu panas.",
 "Pada suatu hari, seorang lelaki yang berdiri di tempat tinggi untuk meninjau menjerit: “Dia sudah sampai! Orang yang kamu tunggu-tunggu sudah sampai!” Semua orang bergegas keluar untuk menyambut baginda. (Bukhari)",
 "Nabi ﷺ tinggal di Quba' selama beberapa hari, dan baginda membina masjid yang pertama sekali dalam Islam di sini. Baginda mengangkat batu dengan tangan baginda sendiri.",
 "Allah memuji masjid ini dalam al-Quran: “masjid yang didirikan atas dasar takwa sejak hari pertama... Di dalamnya ada orang-orang yang suka membersihkan dan menyucikan diri.” (At-Taubah 9:108)",
 "Walaupun selepas baginda berpindah ke dalam kota, Nabi ﷺ suka menziarahi Quba' setiap hari Sabtu, kadang-kadang berjalan kaki dan kadang-kadang menunggang, lalu solat 2 rakaat. (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Baginda bersabda bahawa sesiapa yang mengambil wuduk di rumah, kemudian datang ke Masjid Quba' dan solat di dalamnya, akan mendapat pahala seperti umrah. (Ibn Majah, An-Nasa'i) Jadi ambillah wuduk di hotel sebelum kamu pergi!"],
 look:["Kubah-kubah putih dan menara-menara putih yang tinggi.","Halaman yang sejuk dan terbuka."],
 think:"Pahala seperti satu umrah, hanya dengan wuduk dan lawatan yang singkat! Allah memberi begitu banyak untuk amalan baik yang kecil. Apakah amalan baik kecil yang boleh kamu lakukan hari ini?"}},

"Date farm · Ajwa":{img:["palm","ajwa"],
 en:{cap:["A date palm full of dates at a farm in Madinah.","Ajwa dates: small, dark and soft."],
 p:["Madinah has been a city of date palms for a very long time. When the Prophet ﷺ arrived, it was full of palm gardens.",
 "There are many kinds of dates. The most famous from Madinah is Ajwa: small, dark, soft and a bit wrinkly. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever eats 7 Ajwa dates in the morning will not be harmed by poison or magic that day.” (Bukhari)",
 "Once, the Prophet ﷺ asked his Companions a riddle: “There is a tree whose leaves don't fall, and it is like a Muslim. Which tree is it?” Young Abdullah ibn Umar knew the answer, but he was too shy to say it, because the older people were quiet. The Prophet ﷺ told them: “It is the date palm.” (Bukhari)",
 "Why is a palm tree like a Muslim? Every part of it is useful. Dates for food, trunks for building, leaves for roofs and mats, and fibre for rope. A good Muslim is useful to others too.",
 "Here is another story. Salman al-Farisi came from Persia, far away. He travelled from teacher to teacher, searching for the truth. He was tricked and sold as a slave, and ended up working on a date farm in Madinah.",
 "When he met the Prophet ﷺ and became Muslim, his master agreed to free him if he planted 300 date palms and paid some gold. The Companions helped dig the holes, and the Prophet ﷺ planted each little palm with his own hands. Not one of them died! (Ahmad)",
 "The Prophet ﷺ liked to break his fast with fresh dates. If there were none, then dried dates. If there were none, then a few sips of water. (Abu Dawud, Tirmidhi)"],
 look:["Bunches of dates hanging high in the palms.","Different dates at the shop: Ajwa, Sukkari, Safawi. Do a taste test!"],
 think:"A Muslim is like a palm tree: strong, useful and always giving. What useful thing could you do for someone today?"},
 ms:{cap:["Pokok kurma yang penuh dengan buah di sebuah ladang di Madinah.","Kurma Ajwa: kecil, gelap dan lembut."],
 p:["Madinah sudah lama menjadi bandar pokok kurma. Apabila Nabi ﷺ tiba, bandar itu penuh dengan kebun kurma.",
 "Ada banyak jenis kurma. Yang paling terkenal dari Madinah ialah Ajwa: kecil, gelap, lembut dan sedikit berkedut. Nabi ﷺ bersabda: “Sesiapa yang makan 7 biji kurma Ajwa pada waktu pagi, dia tidak akan dimudaratkan oleh racun atau sihir pada hari itu.” (Bukhari)",
 "Pada suatu hari, Nabi ﷺ memberi teka-teki kepada para sahabat: “Ada sebatang pokok yang daunnya tidak gugur, dan ia seperti seorang Muslim. Pokok apakah itu?” Abdullah bin Umar yang masih muda tahu jawapannya, tetapi dia terlalu malu untuk menjawab, kerana orang-orang yang lebih tua diam sahaja. Nabi ﷺ memberitahu mereka: “Ia ialah pokok kurma.” (Bukhari)",
 "Mengapa pokok kurma seperti seorang Muslim? Setiap bahagiannya berguna. Buahnya untuk makanan, batangnya untuk binaan, daunnya untuk bumbung dan tikar, dan seratnya untuk tali. Seorang Muslim yang baik juga berguna kepada orang lain.",
 "Ini satu lagi kisah. Salman al-Farisi datang dari Parsi, yang sangat jauh. Dia mengembara dari seorang guru ke guru yang lain, mencari kebenaran. Dia ditipu dan dijual sebagai hamba, dan akhirnya bekerja di sebuah ladang kurma di Madinah.",
 "Apabila dia bertemu Nabi ﷺ dan memeluk Islam, tuannya bersetuju untuk membebaskannya jika dia menanam 300 pokok kurma dan membayar sejumlah emas. Para sahabat membantu menggali lubang, dan Nabi ﷺ menanam setiap anak pokok kurma itu dengan tangan baginda sendiri. Tidak ada satu pun yang mati! (Ahmad)",
 "Nabi ﷺ suka berbuka puasa dengan kurma segar. Jika tiada, dengan kurma kering. Jika tiada juga, dengan beberapa teguk air. (Abu Dawud, Tirmidhi)"],
 look:["Tandan-tandan kurma yang tergantung tinggi pada pokok.","Pelbagai jenis kurma di kedai: Ajwa, Sukkari, Safawi. Cubalah rasa semuanya!"],
 think:"Seorang Muslim seperti pokok kurma: kuat, berguna dan sentiasa memberi. Apakah perkara berguna yang boleh kamu lakukan untuk seseorang hari ini?"}},

"Uhud":{img:["uhud","uhud-plain"],
 en:{cap:["Mount Uhud, the big reddish mountain north of Madinah.","The open ground at the foot of Uhud, where the battle happened."],
 p:["Uhud is the big reddish mountain just north of Madinah.",
 "In the year 3 AH, an army of 3,000 from Makkah came to attack Madinah. The Muslims had only about 700.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ put 50 archers on a small hill, now called Jabal Rumah, the Archers' Hill. He told them: “Don't leave this hill, even if you see birds snatching us away!” (Bukhari)",
 "At first, the Muslims were winning, and the enemy ran away. Many archers thought the battle was over. They came down to collect the things the enemy had left behind. Their leader reminded them of the order, but most of them left anyway.",
 "Khalid ibn al-Walid, who was not yet a Muslim, saw that the hill was empty. He rode around with his horsemen and attacked from behind. The Muslims were taken by surprise, and the Prophet ﷺ himself was hurt.",
 "70 Companions were martyred that day, which means they died in the way of Allah. One of them was the Prophet's ﷺ brave uncle Hamzah, called “the Lion of Allah”. They are buried here, near the mountain.",
 "Khalid later became a Muslim, and one of the greatest leaders in Islam.",
 "Even after that sad day, the Prophet ﷺ loved this mountain. He said: “Uhud is a mountain that loves us, and we love it.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Once he climbed Uhud with Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, and the mountain shook. He said: “Be still, Uhud! On you are a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.” (Bukhari)"],
 look:["Jabal Rumah, the small Archers' Hill. Can you see why it mattered?","The graveyard of the martyrs of Uhud, behind its fence. Say salam to them.","The red-brown rocks of Mount Uhud."],
 think:"Why do you think the archers left the hill? What can we learn about listening to good advice, even when it seems the danger is over?"},
 ms:{cap:["Bukit Uhud, bukit besar berwarna kemerahan di utara Madinah.","Kawasan lapang di kaki Bukit Uhud, tempat peperangan itu berlaku."],
 p:["Uhud ialah bukit besar berwarna kemerahan di sebelah utara Madinah.",
 "Pada tahun 3 H, sebuah tentera seramai 3,000 orang dari Makkah datang untuk menyerang Madinah. Orang Islam hanya kira-kira 700 orang.",
 "Nabi ﷺ menempatkan 50 orang pemanah di atas sebuah bukit kecil, yang kini dipanggil Jabal Rumah, Bukit Pemanah. Baginda berpesan kepada mereka: “Jangan tinggalkan bukit ini, walaupun kamu melihat burung-burung menyambar kami!” (Bukhari)",
 "Pada mulanya, orang Islam sedang menang, dan musuh melarikan diri. Ramai pemanah menyangka peperangan sudah tamat. Mereka turun untuk mengutip barang-barang yang ditinggalkan oleh musuh. Ketua mereka mengingatkan mereka tentang perintah itu, tetapi kebanyakan mereka tetap pergi.",
 "Khalid bin al-Walid, yang belum memeluk Islam ketika itu, ternampak bukit itu sudah kosong. Dia membawa pasukan berkudanya berpusing dan menyerang dari belakang. Orang Islam terkejut, dan Nabi ﷺ sendiri tercedera.",
 "70 orang sahabat syahid pada hari itu, maksudnya mereka meninggal dunia di jalan Allah. Salah seorang daripada mereka ialah bapa saudara Nabi ﷺ yang berani, Hamzah, yang digelar “Singa Allah”. Mereka dikebumikan di sini, berhampiran bukit ini.",
 "Khalid kemudiannya memeluk Islam, dan menjadi salah seorang pemimpin yang paling hebat dalam Islam.",
 "Walaupun selepas hari yang menyedihkan itu, Nabi ﷺ tetap menyayangi bukit ini. Baginda bersabda: “Uhud ialah bukit yang mencintai kita, dan kita mencintainya.” (Bukhari, Muslim)",
 "Pada suatu hari, baginda mendaki Uhud bersama Saidina Abu Bakar, Umar dan Uthman, lalu bukit itu bergegar. Baginda bersabda: “Tenanglah, wahai Uhud! Di atasmu ada seorang Nabi, seorang yang benar, dan dua orang syahid.” (Bukhari)"],
 look:["Jabal Rumah, Bukit Pemanah yang kecil. Bolehkah kamu nampak mengapa ia penting?","Tanah perkuburan para syuhada Uhud, di sebalik pagarnya. Ucapkan salam kepada mereka.","Batu-batu merah keperangan di Bukit Uhud."],
 think:"Pada pendapat kamu, mengapa para pemanah meninggalkan bukit itu? Apakah yang boleh kita pelajari tentang mendengar nasihat yang baik, walaupun bahaya nampaknya sudah berlalu?"}},

"Masjid Qiblatayn":{img:["qiblatayn"],
 en:{cap:["The entrance of Masjid Qiblatayn in Madinah."],
 p:["The qiblah is the direction we face when we pray. Today it is the Kaaba in Makkah. But in the early years, the Muslims faced Masjid Al-Aqsa in Jerusalem.",
 "After moving to Madinah, they faced Jerusalem for 16 or 17 months. (Bukhari) The Prophet ﷺ loved the Kaaba and hoped to face it. He would often look up at the sky, waiting for Allah's command.",
 "Then Allah revealed: “We have seen you turning your face to the sky. So We will turn you to a qiblah that pleases you. Turn your face towards Al-Masjid Al-Haram.” (Al-Baqarah 2:144)",
 "The news spread fast. A man who had prayed with the Prophet ﷺ passed some people who were in the middle of their prayer. He called out that the qiblah had changed. They turned around, right there in the middle of their prayer, to face the Kaaba! (Bukhari)",
 "Jerusalem is north of Madinah and Makkah is south, so they had to turn almost all the way around!",
 "Qiblatayn means “two qiblahs”. This mosque is traditionally said to be where people turned like this, and that is how it got its name. An authentic report also tells of people in Masjid Quba' turning during Fajr when they heard the news.",
 "Masjid Al-Aqsa is still very special. It is the third holiest masjid in Islam, and the place the Prophet ﷺ travelled to on the Night Journey."],
 look:["The white minarets and domes.","Inside, the mihrab facing Makkah. Which way would Jerusalem be?"],
 think:"Those people turned the moment they heard Allah's command. Do you do good things straight away when you hear them?"},
 ms:{cap:["Pintu masuk Masjid Qiblatain di Madinah."],
 p:["Kiblat ialah arah yang kita hadap ketika solat. Hari ini kiblat ialah Kaabah di Makkah. Tetapi pada tahun-tahun awal, orang Islam menghadap Masjidil Aqsa di Baitulmaqdis.",
 "Selepas berpindah ke Madinah, mereka menghadap Baitulmaqdis selama 16 atau 17 bulan. (Bukhari) Nabi ﷺ menyayangi Kaabah dan berharap dapat menghadapnya. Baginda selalu mendongak ke langit, menunggu perintah Allah.",
 "Kemudian Allah menurunkan ayat: “Kami telah melihat mukamu berulang kali menengadah ke langit. Maka Kami akan palingkan engkau ke kiblat yang engkau sukai. Palingkanlah mukamu ke arah Masjidil Haram.” (Al-Baqarah 2:144)",
 "Berita itu tersebar dengan cepat. Seorang lelaki yang telah solat bersama Nabi ﷺ melalui sekumpulan orang yang sedang solat. Dia berseru bahawa kiblat telah berubah. Mereka terus berpusing, di situ juga ketika masih solat, untuk menghadap Kaabah! (Bukhari)",
 "Baitulmaqdis terletak di utara Madinah dan Makkah di selatan, jadi mereka terpaksa berpusing hampir sepenuhnya ke belakang!",
 "Qiblatain bermaksud “dua kiblat”. Menurut cerita turun-temurun, masjid inilah tempat orang berpusing seperti itu, dan dari situlah datangnya namanya. Satu riwayat yang sahih juga menceritakan tentang orang di Masjid Quba' yang berpusing ketika solat Subuh apabila mendengar berita itu.",
 "Masjidil Aqsa masih sangat istimewa. Ia masjid ketiga paling suci dalam Islam, dan tempat yang dikunjungi Nabi ﷺ dalam peristiwa Israk."],
 look:["Menara-menara dan kubah-kubah putih.","Di dalam, mihrab yang menghadap Makkah. Ke arah manakah Baitulmaqdis?"],
 think:"Orang-orang itu terus berpusing sebaik sahaja mendengar perintah Allah. Adakah kamu terus membuat perkara baik sebaik sahaja kamu mendengarnya?"}},

"Baqi'":{img:["baqi"],
 en:{cap:["Al-Baqi', the main graveyard of Madinah, next to Masjid An-Nabawi."],
 p:["Al-Baqi' is the main graveyard of Madinah, right next to Masjid An-Nabawi. It has been used since the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and thousands of Companions are buried here.",
 "One of them is Uthman ibn Affan, the third khalifah. He was very generous. He bought a well called Bi'r Rumah so that everyone in Madinah could drink for free. (Bukhari) He also gathered the Quran into one book, and had copies sent to faraway lands.",
 "Many of the Prophet's ﷺ wives, the Mothers of the Believers, are buried here too.",
 "So is his baby son Ibrahim, who died when he was very little. The Prophet ﷺ cried, and said: “The eyes shed tears and the heart is sad, but we only say what pleases our Lord.” (Bukhari) It is OK to feel sad. Even the Prophet ﷺ cried.",
 "The Prophet ﷺ sometimes came to Baqi' at night to make dua for the people buried here. (Muslim)",
 "The graves are simple mounds of earth with small stones. In Islam, graves are kept plain.",
 "When you pass by, say: “Assalamu 'alaikum ahlad-diyar...” It means: “Peace be upon you, people of these homes, believers and Muslims. We will join you, if Allah wills. We ask Allah for well-being for us and for you.” (Muslim)",
 "Usually only men can go inside, at set times. Anyone can say salam from outside the wall."],
 look:["The simple graves, each marked with small stones.","The minarets of Masjid An-Nabawi right beside it."],
 think:"Visiting graves reminds us that life is short. What good thing would you like people to remember you for?"},
 ms:{cap:["Al-Baqi', tanah perkuburan utama di Madinah, di sebelah Masjid Nabawi."],
 p:["Al-Baqi' ialah tanah perkuburan utama di Madinah, betul-betul di sebelah Masjid Nabawi. Ia telah digunakan sejak zaman Nabi ﷺ, dan beribu-ribu sahabat dikebumikan di sini.",
 "Salah seorang daripada mereka ialah Saidina Uthman bin Affan, khalifah yang ketiga. Dia sangat pemurah. Dia membeli sebuah perigi bernama Bi'r Rumah supaya semua penduduk Madinah boleh minum secara percuma. (Bukhari) Dia juga mengumpulkan al-Quran dalam satu kitab, dan menghantar salinannya ke negeri-negeri yang jauh.",
 "Ramai isteri Nabi ﷺ, iaitu para Ummul Mukminin (ibu orang-orang yang beriman), juga dikebumikan di sini.",
 "Begitu juga anak lelaki baginda, Ibrahim, yang meninggal dunia ketika masih bayi. Nabi ﷺ menangis, dan bersabda: “Mata menitiskan air mata dan hati berasa sedih, tetapi kami hanya mengucapkan apa yang diredai oleh Tuhan kami.” (Bukhari) Tidak mengapa berasa sedih. Nabi ﷺ pun menangis.",
 "Nabi ﷺ kadang-kadang datang ke Baqi' pada waktu malam untuk mendoakan orang-orang yang dikebumikan di sini. (Muslim)",
 "Kubur-kuburnya hanyalah timbunan tanah yang ringkas dengan batu-batu kecil. Dalam Islam, kubur dibiarkan ringkas.",
 "Apabila kamu lalu di situ, ucapkanlah: “Assalamu 'alaikum ahlad-diyar...” Maksudnya: “Salam sejahtera ke atas kamu, wahai penghuni kediaman ini, daripada kalangan orang beriman dan orang Islam. Kami akan menyusul kamu, insya-Allah. Kami memohon kepada Allah kesejahteraan untuk kami dan untuk kamu.” (Muslim)",
 "Biasanya hanya lelaki boleh masuk ke dalam, pada waktu-waktu tertentu. Sesiapa pun boleh mengucapkan salam dari luar tembok."],
 look:["Kubur-kubur yang ringkas, setiap satu ditandai dengan batu-batu kecil.","Menara-menara Masjid Nabawi betul-betul di sebelahnya."],
 think:"Menziarahi kubur mengingatkan kita bahawa hidup ini singkat. Apakah kebaikan yang kamu mahu orang ingat tentang diri kamu?"}}
};
